    {
      "filename": "San Gregorio State Beach (8406319801).jpg",
      "title": "File:San Gregorio State Beach (8406319801).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4b/San_Gregorio_State_Beach_%288406319801%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:San_Gregorio_State_Beach_(8406319801).jpg",
      "width": 1648,
      "height": 1097,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "jason jenkins from stockton, california",
      "description": "San Gregorio State Beach San Mateo County coast. This image was one of my first shots on this beach during a meet up with Lorenzo Montezemolo. I actually got caught inside the tidal wash in this image and became drenched from the knee down as 10-15 foot waves crashed just offshore. I wont forget Lorenzo Yelling \"Here it Comes!\" as i composed the shot with my back to the ocean.(bad idea) It was worth it and luckily the water felt great on this nearly perfect 70 degree day.I was attracted to the texture of this rock and i knew a long exposure was perfect for the scene. Once the tide came in there would be a beautiful contrast between soft, smooth moving water against a solid surface. I waited for the right moment as the sun began to light the rock my wave came in and created the scene.\n\n::Tech details::\n\nSingle Image (non HDR)\nShutter 3.2 seconds\nAperture F11\nISO 100\nfocal length 18mm\nHoya ND 64 filter\ntripod\nSony Alpha a390 DSLR\n\nSony 18-55mm F3.5-5.6SAM lens",
      "dateCreated": "2013-01-19 18:15",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "san-gregorio-state-beach-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "9q8u",
      "smallPath": "_m/9/q/8/u/san-gregorio-state-beach-wp/san-gregorio-state-beach-84063-small.webp"
    },
